  "term": "dispersal",
  "definition": "Dispersal is the spreading of the seeds, eggs, embryos, or spores of plants and relatively fixed animals across a wider area. In this historical usage, it happens through forces such as wind, water currents, or animals, and some species have structures that help or limit that spread.",
